          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"category\":\"widespread waveform-feature or AutoDQM reference mismatch\",\"cause\":\"unknown; leading hypothesis is a detector-wide pulse-feature processing, configuration, or reference-baseline incompatibility rather than a localized LVDS/PMT failure\",\"action\":\"First verify raw waveforms and recompute pulse statistics for representative affected and unflagged channels, checking for zero/constant medians, invalid values, pulse-finder settings, thresholds, calibration versions, and compatibility with the AutoDQM reference. Compare digitizer event rates against trigger-board rates and inspect board matching, synchronization, queue occupancy, and DAQ restart/configuration logs. If raw data are normal, correct the feature extraction or reference normalization; if raw data show a board-correlated acquisition fault, restart or resynchronize only the implicated DAQ component after preserving diagnostics.\",\"confidence\":0.48,\"supporting_historical_runs\":[1605,1642,2126],\"reasoning_summary\":\"OBSERVED: anomalies affect every subrun and produce 10,816 channel-entries, with several pulse-count and pulse-shape features reaching exact extreme z-scores. Trigger rate remains near 4.86 Hz, while LVDS has no persistent zero, missing, high, or low signal pins. The final count drops occur in both trigger and LVDS totals and may reflect a shorter subrun. INFERRED: the detector-wide persistence, nominal trigger rate, and healthy aggregate LVDS pattern argue against a single broken PMT base, isolated LVDS connection, or high-trigger-rate condition; exact million-scale z-scores may indicate degenerate reference variance or pathological feature values. Runs 1605, 1642, and 2126 partially resemble the affected channels or extreme nPulses scores, but had different confirmed problems, so there is no exact historical match. UNKNOWN: raw waveform quality, digitizer rates, board matching, synchronization, queue state, within-run configuration, and whether anomalies cluster by digitizer. These checks are required to distinguish analysis/reference failure from a widespread DAQ acquisition fault.\"}"
        }
      ],
